WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.313
Welcome to Dino Dynasty!

2
00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:10.708
In this video you will learn how to play by watching a real game against the computer, one step at a time.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.692
Your goal is to build the best dino park in fifteen rounds.

4
00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:22.072
You draw fences to make enclosures, buy dinos to live in them, keep them fed, and chase goal cards.

5
00:00:22.072 --> 00:00:24.627
Whoever has the most points at the end wins.

6
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.004
This is the home page.

7
00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:33.400
The Game lobby button at the top left takes you back to all the board games,

8
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.725
and the music button at the top right turns the game’s music on or off.

9
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.511
First, pick how you want to play: against the computer, two players sharing one device,

10
00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:48.473
or online against a friend. We will play against the computer.

11
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.337
Choose how hard the computer is and how fast it moves.

12
00:00:53.337 --> 00:00:57.200
Then pick who goes first: you, the computer, or a random pick.

13
00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.755
We will go first, and press Start game.

14
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.543
Each round begins with a new event card.

15
00:01:06.543 --> 00:01:10.875
This one is Payday: coins spaces give 2 more coins this round.

16
00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:13.088
Events never repeat in a game.

17
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.204
Then the first goal card is revealed.

18
00:01:16.204 --> 00:01:19.320
Goals score points at the end of the game for everybody.

19
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.688
A second goal appears in round six, and the last one in round eleven.

20
00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:30.041
The panel on the right always shows the four steps of the round: Food and Fences, Workers,

21
00:01:30.041 --> 00:01:33.343
Production, and Feeding. Press Start round to begin.

22
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.427
Step one is Food and Fences. One die is rolled for both players.

23
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.305
We rolled a six. You split that number between food and fences.

24
00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:49.933
Food is meat for meat eaters, and plants for plant eaters.

25
00:01:49.933 --> 00:01:53.320
Each fence fills one dotted edge of a square on your board.

26
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.865
An enclosure is an area completely closed off by fences.

27
00:01:58.865 --> 00:02:03.027
The edge of the board can count as a wall, but on two sides at most.

28
00:02:03.027 --> 00:02:06.328
Here, three fences close off two squares in the corner.

29
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.311
We spend the other three points on meat, because the dino we want eats meat.

30
00:02:12.311 --> 00:02:13.948
Then press Confirm.

31
00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.801
Step two is Workers. You have three workers each round.

32
00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:27.300
Players take turns placing one worker at a time on an action space and doing what it says.

33
00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.860
Every action comes in three tiers.

34
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.493
The top and middle spaces hold only one worker per round, so taking one blocks your opponent.

35
00:02:36.493 --> 00:02:40.371
The bottom space is weaker, but any number of workers can use it.

36
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.500
The actions are: play a dino, breed, take coins, buy diamonds, forage for food,

37
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.359
draw fences, build feeders and watering holes, and scout to reserve cards.

38
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.188
Let us play a dino. We put our first worker on the top Play a dino space.

39
00:02:58.188 --> 00:03:01.660
Now every dino we can afford lights up in the market.

40
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.679
Each card shows its points in the corner, its cost, how many squares it takes,

41
00:03:07.679 --> 00:03:09.835
what it eats, and the coins it earns.

42
00:03:09.835 --> 00:03:15.056
The coloured bar tells you when its power works: when played, every round, or at the end.

43
00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.492
The little picture on the art is the dino’s shape: the exact squares it fills,

44
00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:24.779
drawn as its silhouette, head in front and legs below.

45
00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:28.364
Small dinos are just a couple of squares, while a big T.

46
00:03:28.364 --> 00:03:31.921
Rex or Mosasaurus is a large, awkward piece.

47
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.135
The Compy costs two coins, takes two squares and eats one meat.

48
00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:41.415
At the end it scores a point for each Compy next to it.

49
00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.329
Now tap a square inside an enclosure, and the whole shape drops there.

50
00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:50.847
Each enclosure holds only one species, unless it has a watering hole.

51
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.959
Like a Tetris piece, you can turn it with Rotate, the R key or a right-click,

52
00:03:56.959 --> 00:03:59.179
and mirror it with Flip or the F key.

53
00:03:59.179 --> 00:04:04.492
Stood on end, our Compy pokes out of the enclosure, so it shows a dashed red outline.

54
00:04:04.492 --> 00:04:06.791
One more turn and it fits again.

55
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.221
Our Compy is in the park! Now the computer places a worker.

56
00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:21.827
It took the top Scout space, to reserve 2 cards, take 1 coin, and go first next round.

57
00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:26.611
With our second worker we take three coins from the top Coins space.

58
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.905
The computer took the middle Play a dino space, to play a dino for 1 coin extra.

59
00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:36.021
We use the middle Fences space to draw four fences.

60
00:04:36.021 --> 00:04:39.451
That makes a second enclosure, ready for our next dino.

61
00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:50.572
Step three is Production. Pick one active enclosure and collect the coins its dinos earn.

62
00:04:50.572 --> 00:04:54.833
After that, every round powers of your dinos trigger by themselves.

63
00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.244
Step four is Feeding.

64
00:04:59.244 --> 00:05:04.152
Each enclosure needs the food its dinos eat, and feeder squares lower that bill.

65
00:05:04.152 --> 00:05:09.636
Until you tap an enclosure to feed it, it is marked in orange with what will happen if you skip it.

66
00:05:09.636 --> 00:05:12.105
Here, our Compy will go inactive.

67
00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.764
Inactive dinos earn nothing, cannot breed, eat even more next time,

68
00:05:18.764 --> 00:05:22.541
and after four hungry rounds in a row they die, shown in red.

69
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:27.485
So tap the enclosure to feed it: our Compy eats one meat. Then confirm.

70
00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.703
That is one full round. In round two the computer goes first,

71
00:05:33.703 --> 00:05:38.227
because it took the top Scout space, two market cards are swapped for new ones,

72
00:05:38.227 --> 00:05:44.045
and a new event arrives: Tax day: everyone loses a third of their coins (rounded down).

73
00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.047
Now let’s go through every rule.

74
00:05:47.047 --> 00:05:51.528
The rules are always one click away, from the Rules button in the top bar.

75
00:05:51.528 --> 00:05:55.448
The first tab is this video, so you can come back to it any time.

76
00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:03.671
You start with an empty twelve by twelve park, five coins, and no food or diamonds.

77
00:06:03.671 --> 00:06:08.792
Diamonds pay for some dinos and buildings, and each one left over is worth a point.

78
00:06:08.792 --> 00:06:11.859
You can hold up to five reserved cards in your hand.

79
00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:21.209
Remember three things. Dinos only live in closed enclosures, one species each.

80
00:06:21.209 --> 00:06:23.515
Feed every enclosure every round.

81
00:06:23.515 --> 00:06:28.053
And points come from dinos, their powers, goals, diamonds and coins.

82
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.564
At the start of each round, an event is revealed,

83
00:06:34.564 --> 00:06:38.448
two market cards are swapped for new ones, a goal may be revealed,

84
00:06:38.448 --> 00:06:40.647
and babies that are ready grow up.

85
00:06:40.647 --> 00:06:45.932
The first player switches, unless someone took the top Scout space, then they go first.

86
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.716
In Food and Fences, fences are permanent, and points you don’t use are lost.

87
00:06:54.716 --> 00:06:58.465
Fences can’t cut through a dino, feeder or watering hole.

88
00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:06.329
In Workers, you may pass instead of placing a worker, but that worker is lost for the round.

89
00:07:06.329 --> 00:07:09.396
You can only use a space if you can do what it says.

90
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.724
In Production, babies earn half, rounded up,

91
00:07:14.724 --> 00:07:20.123
and every-round powers of adult dinos in active enclosures trigger one at a time.

92
00:07:20.123 --> 00:07:23.147
After the feeding of round fifteen, the game ends.

93
00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.852
Here is every worker space, with its top, middle and bottom tier.

94
00:07:29.852 --> 00:07:33.885
Play a dino costs one or two coins extra on the lower tiers.

95
00:07:33.885 --> 00:07:38.147
Breed is free on top, three coins in the middle, and six on the bottom.

96
00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:48.156
Coins gives three, two or one coin. Gems sells a diamond for five, six or seven coins.

97
00:07:48.156 --> 00:07:53.633
Forage gives four, three or one food, and Fences draws five, four or two fences.

98
00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:02.495
Builder builds one feeder, for a diamond plus a coin per square, or one watering hole,

99
00:08:02.495 --> 00:08:05.696
for a diamond and two coins, taking six squares.

100
00:08:05.696 --> 00:08:11.152
Scout reserves cards; reserved cards cost a coin less, and only you can buy them.

101
00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.447
An enclosure may use at most two sides of the board edge.

102
00:08:18.447 --> 00:08:24.144
Each dino fills its own shape, turned or flipped any way you like, inside one enclosure.

103
00:08:24.144 --> 00:08:27.367
Feeders and watering holes fill connected squares.

104
00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:32.012
Each enclosure holds one species, plus one more for every watering hole.

105
00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.263
Each feeder square takes one food off that enclosure’s bill.

106
00:08:40.263 --> 00:08:43.080
You can split an enclosure later with new fences.

107
00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:47.235
Squares filled in by a Storm or a Spinosaurus are blocked for good.

108
00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.993
An unfed enclosure goes inactive with a marker on one.

109
00:08:53.993 --> 00:09:00.864
Each of its dinos eats extra food equal to the marker, and the marker rises every feeding it stays unfed.

110
00:09:00.864 --> 00:09:02.828
Feed it in full to wake it up.

111
00:09:02.828 --> 00:09:08.625
Unfed with the marker on four, its dinos die, and the enclosure is extinct forever.

112
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:18.276
To breed, you need an adult pair of one species in an active enclosure,

113
00:09:18.276 --> 00:09:20.859
and each enclosure breeds once per round.

114
00:09:20.859 --> 00:09:26.556
Babies take the first half of the shape, and eat, earn and score half. After two feedings,

115
00:09:26.556 --> 00:09:30.227
or one with an adult Maiasaura, they grow up next round,

116
00:09:30.227 --> 00:09:32.611
if the full shape fits over the baby.

117
00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:42.596
The All dinos tab shows every card and exactly what its power does.

118
00:09:42.596 --> 00:09:46.459
Powers work when played, every round, or at the end. A T.

119
00:09:46.459 --> 00:09:50.976
Rex can block a species from being bought or bred until the block ends.

120
00:09:54.840 --> 00:10:00.452
At the end of round fifteen you score each dino’s points, scoring powers like the Compy’s,

121
00:10:00.452 --> 00:10:03.952
all three goal cards, one point per leftover diamond,

122
00:10:03.952 --> 00:10:10.219
and one point per ten leftover coins, up to three. Only dinos in active enclosures count.

123
00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:19.873
There are fifteen possible goal cards, like Big herds, Oasis and Treasury.

124
00:10:19.873 --> 00:10:24.327
Three are used each game, and they all score, even one revealed late.

125
00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.767
Finally, the events. Some help, like Feast and Payday.

126
00:10:30.767 --> 00:10:33.648
Some hurt, like Tax day, Storm and Heatwave.

127
00:10:33.648 --> 00:10:37.739
Each one lasts a single round, and none comes up twice in a game.

128
00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:45.844
During the game, tap any goal card to see what it is worth for you right now,

129
00:10:45.844 --> 00:10:50.276
What happened to see every move, and Lobby to go back to all the board games.

130
00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:57.287
Remember: close your enclosures, keep every dino fed, and watch the goal cards.

131
00:10:57.287 --> 00:11:01.299
When the game ends, the scores are revealed one category at a time.

132
00:11:01.299 --> 00:11:05.887
Your game saves as you play, and when you are signed in it is kept in your account,

133
00:11:05.887 --> 00:11:10.084
so you can carry on from any device. Have fun building your park!

